{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113343-starting-a-chronicle-in-a-week-any-advice","id":1113343,"title":"Starting a chronicle in a week, any advice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-08T13:15:32-07:00","id":1113343,"title":"Starting a chronicle in a week, any advice?","content":"I'll be running M20 in a week. It'll be the first time I've run a WOD game ever. Anybody have any practical advice for me? I've got an idea for the big-bads for the game, but I'll need help statting them out. I'll share my idea for them later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T14:54:17-07:00","id":1113396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113343-starting-a-chronicle-in-a-week-any-advice#post1113343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be running M20 in a week. It'll be the first time I've run a WOD game ever. Anybody have any practical advice for me? I've got an idea for the big-bads for the game, but I'll need help statting them out. I'll share my idea for them later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my advice, don't worry too much about stating up your NPCs. Just think about what they might be capable of and roll the appropriate number of dice for it. <br /> <br /> Other than that, keep careful note on everyone's decisions, and make sure you plan some suitable consequences for it later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T20:58:35-07:00","id":1113538,"title":"","content":"Think of the game you want to run; the emotions you wanna evoke, the pacing, the mood, the tone. Now make a small list of themes--maybe in the form of key words or maybe just images you could stick to a virtual image board or copy/paste into a word document (I often have the names of movies, characters from fiction, scenes from specific movies, or sometimes just clever ads or album covers). Maybe even prepare a short plain statement describing how you would want your players to describe your game, elevator pitch style.<br /> <br /> Now, whenever you run into a snag in the game--something that requires that you shoot from the hip or cobble together a scene, character, problem, or solution on the fly... look at your word doc/image board/mission statement/whatever. This always helps to re-focus me onto the core milieu of my game, and (it is my belief that) it helps keep whatever rando decision I make stay tonally consistent. That said, over time, after the game has developed its own personality, informed not only by your creative vision, but the players' as well, this reference tool may become less useful (though I always reference mine when planning the next major story arc).<br /> <br /> Hope this helps! Good luck and have fun!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T02:49:53-07:00","id":1113668,"title":"","content":"What stage are the players starting at? Do they know the setting at all? <br /> Saikou gave some good advice to another new storyteller in the thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1112358-new-member-with-some-probably-noobish-questions\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...bish-questions</a> - build some of your plot out of your characters' backstories to have a reason to bring them together and care about each other. <br /> If your players are all new to the setting, consider doing an awakening chronicle like I have: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1106465-newbies-campaign-creative-input-requested\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...nput-requested</a><br /> <br /> I've found this forum very useful while brainstorming as well so do post your ideas up for criticism and help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T15:08:50-07:00","id":1113890,"title":"","content":"Make sure the players make characters who can <i>and will</i> work together. They can have personal plots, but there should be a reason the players are at the table at the same time. This is useful in most games, of course, but it's particularly pertinent in games where the characters can have wildly divergent worldviews and agendas. Likewise, find out what the players want to do, and what their characters want as well, which may be very different things!<br /> <br /> Introduce the setting bits at a time. Get a hang of the Traditions and Technocracy, and how they operate unseen in the mundane world, before bringing in Marauders, Nephandi, spirit realms and zeppelins. Similarly, don't feel the need to include everything - a low-key game about a casual cabal who meet at a coffee shop in San Francisco might not be the best place for those zeppelins to show up.<br /> <br /> There aren't many published adventures available. <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/131409/Mage-20th-Anniversary-Edition-Quickstart\" target=\"_blank\">The free M20 quickstart</a> includes a cabal of characters with plot hooks built in, rather than a ready-to-run adventure.<br /> <br /> There are also adventures for first edition: the intro adventure <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/190/Loom-of-Fate\" target=\"_blank\">Loom Of Fate</a>, another shorter intro adventure in <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/3590/White-Wolf-Magazine-37\" target=\"_blank\">White Wolf Magazine</a> 37 and the famously over-the-top <b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</b> crossover <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/57/Chaos-Factor\" target=\"_blank\">Chaos Factor</a> - you can get Loom and Chaos in <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/196/Mage-Chronicles-Volume-3\" target=\"_blank\">this collection</a>.<br /> <br /> And for Revised there's the <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> crossover <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/37/Blood-Treachery\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Treachery</a>, and the &quot;end of the world&quot; book <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1718/Ascension\" target=\"_blank\">Ascension</a> containing five adventures featuring different ways to end the setting.<br /> <br /> That said, Mages could investigate the strange happenings in many modern horror adventures, including ones for the <b>World Of Darkness</b> and <b>Chronicles Of Darkness</b> lines as well as other RPGs - as long as you're prepared to adjust statistics as required, and consider their power level compared to &quot;average joe&quot; monster hunters as they face their enemies with arcane knowledge and mystical powers rather than blind faith and shotguns. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T21:20:37-07:00","id":1116698,"title":"","content":"It went well. I got everyone up to speed on the rules and we did character gen. As it was very late near the end I let them do freebies over this next week so they would have time to look through all the goodies in the Book of Secrets. We'll begin the game next week with their awakening and training as mages. By the way, has anyone come up with particularly interesting awakenings for a Chorister, Hollow One, Ecstatic or Hermetic? I want to really wow them with their awakening but material on that subject seems almost nonexistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T21:36:11-07:00","id":1116710,"title":"","content":"Awakenings are very personal. They need to be experiences, like Seekings, where mages realize that reality is not what it is. They need to be transformative experiences.<br /> <br /> If we go by the groups, a Chorister is primarily empowered by their faith in the One. So, some religious revelation would be in order. Hollow Ones are a particular brand of 'orphan,' and tend to tie into the gothic culture in Mage lore. So, for the Hollow One, they'd probably be thumbing their nose at authority or having some ironic realization. The Ecstatic is from a tradition that's about experiences that are mind-blowing and assuming they take Time as their affinity sphere, you'd want some experience where their sense of time is jarred.<br /> <br /> The Hermetic is the most interesting and difficult case. See, the Order of Hermes comes into Mage from Ars Magica, so you have many different little groups and practices blending into western occultism and studious learners of magic. A Hermetic will typically awaken after years of study, moving from just going through magical rituals to performing minor magics ala a sorcerer to Awakening. However, depending on the House, this could be through doing magic tied to the fae, magic tied to sacred numbers, and so many other things. The Order of Hermes is one of my two favorite traditions (the other being the Sons of Ether) because there are a lot of common beliefs but the Hermetic can have many different connections due to their houses.<br /> <br /> The<i> Initiates of the Arts</i> book from Mage Revised might provide some further ideas on Awakenings. <br /> <br /> If there are four players, perhaps you could have them work with you in pairs on their Awakenings if the character concepts mesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T00:20:38-07:00","id":1116751,"title":"","content":"Important note on the Chorus:<br /> Its not only about &quot;The One.&quot; Or rather, it is, but their faith isnt only from religion. <br /> <br /> The chorus hear music in creation. A faint buzzing sound that lets them hear the tune of the universe. A catholic might hear the faint sound of a choir chanting in latin, while a muslim might hear the muezzin (hopefully didnt butcher the spelling.) <br /> <br /> If I were running an awakening for a choruster, I'd have the event be mainly him starting to hear the noises. If he specilizes in matter, for example, every rock would be singing. Itd be overwhelming at first. The universe itself is singing and its a cacophony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11894-shushu","name":"Shushu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T00:40:08-07:00","id":1116756,"title":"","content":"Regarding the hermetic, yes the vast majority of them are awakened &quot;internally&quot;, but I happen to be reading the tradition book just now and in house ex miscellanea it says quite explicitly that you just need to be awakened and inclined toward hermetic high ritual to become a member. So as long as the awakening involves seeing the world through a hermetic paradigm, they can get &quot;in&quot; later. Access to one of the great houses would be considerably harder, and being outside the give-and-take political games will bring challenge, but most hermetics left on earth after the avatar storm are starved for new recruits. Who's to say they can't find a mentor to take a chance on them, crude outsider though they may be?<br /> <br /> Oh, and what would that look like? Imagine the matrix if instead of seeing ordinary code they saw the world as true names, glyphs and symbols such as seen in Hellblazer and other Alan Moore-related comics, or seeing the corruption of the world in need of the divine light of the flambeau version of ascension, etc. <br /> In addition, to &quot;grease the wheels&quot;, I'd probably have the character choose quite a strong avatar and have the avatar know things from a previous hermetic incarnation, such as a little enochian or the like, to make hermetics treat the character more like a prodigy and give more leeway to them for an Orphan awakening. <br /> <br /> Re: Hollow Ones, while they are often nihilistic, they are categorically not just goths these days. They seem to couple their magic together from pop culture. There's some great sample characters at the back of their &quot;tradition book&quot; if you have access to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13587,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","user":"Eyrelliah","date":".  Submitted too early 07-16-2017, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T10:11:44-07:00","id":1116882,"title":"","content":"It wasn't clear what era the game was set in. The Order of Hermes has centuries of history and the Avatar Storm's impacts, if any, depend on the chronicle.<br /> <br /> I have both the Mage 1e and Mage Revised Tradition books and find the former much more interesting and informative than the latter. You get a lot of variety with the 1e book and the tone is far less grimdark than a group of broken houses hanging on. That being said, if you're into the themes,<i> Blood Treachery</i> was an excellent book for the Order of Hermes fighting a war against the Tremere.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T12:15:20-07:00","id":1117358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113343-starting-a-chronicle-in-a-week-any-advice?p=1116882#post1116882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't clear what era the game was set in. The Order of Hermes has centuries of history and the Avatar Storm's impacts, if any, depend on the chronicle.<br /> <br /> I have both the Mage 1e and Mage Revised Tradition books and find the former much more interesting and informative than the latter. You get a lot of variety with the 1e book and the tone is far less grimdark than a group of broken houses hanging on. That being said, if you're into the themes,<i> Blood Treachery</i> was an excellent book for the Order of Hermes fighting a war against the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies if it seemed like I was directly contradicting you there - that wasn't my intention. I got excited and wanted to splurge my recent discovery :-)<br /> I've never looked at 1st ed, I only know it from the disparaging remarks made about it online and in the intro to the &quot;guide to the technocracy&quot;. <br /> What's lacking from the new books in your view?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T13:53:16-07:00","id":1117423,"title":"","content":"Mage 1e was much more open-ended and you could do more powerful magic without having Paradox eat you for lunch. Also, since it was closer to the time Ars Magica was published, you got more of a flavor of the Hermetic history. The Order of Hermes in Ars Magica, published by Lion Rampant and later White Wolf, ends up being important to early Mage because you get the mages. You also see what Tremere was in the Order of Hermes in Ars Magica and how it becomes the clan in Vampire.<br /> <br /> Mage 2e, especially the Guide to the Technocracy, is furthering the idea in Mage 1e but running it a bit more cleanly and with some better information on the factions. If you want the Technocracy as decent people, the Guide to the Technocracy was great at making Technocrats playable as heroes or more believable as antagonists. The Technocracy was humanized.<br /> <br /> Mage Revised, especially the Avatar Storm and nastier Paradox, restrict player options. For the Order of Hermes, several Houses are gone or weakened, because the fall of Doisstep and Horizon and other chantries cuts off the masters from everyone else. So, if one is playing a Hermetic, which history you use matters a lot.<br /> <br /> As for the Mage Revised books many things about them are good, but they are far too declensionist for my tastes. Everything is moving towards the Apocalypse in both the fiction and the rules, creating a more grimdark World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> I've owned most of the material for Mage in digital form or print form over the years and recently picked up Mage 20. I like the blending of the good ideas from the various editions, as well as the sidebar options for how to handle the metaplot.<br /> <br /> For The OP and anyone else running a chronicle, unless your group is going to completely follow a metaplot or is rules-restricted like the Camarilla is, it is best to figure out what you want and take the seasonings of Mage that work for that. Rule 0 of any game should be the person running the game is always right, with the entailed duty to do right by those other participants in the game by taking into account their tastes and being fair.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T22:50:16-07:00","id":1118082,"title":"","content":"There's a plot structure in urban fantasy that has become pretty standard: a bad thing manifests itself and threatens the status quo; the protagonists use occult lore to research the thing, locate the thing, and then eliminate the thing, restoring the status quo. That is fine if you are running a Technocracy game--for the most part the Technocrats are statusing the hell out of the quo. But mystic mages are an aberration. Their mere existence represents upheaval to reality as we know it. Tradition games and Orphan games are better done when the protagonists are proactive rather than reactive, remaking the world in their image.<br /> <br /> There is also a practical reason for attempting to go beyond the urban fantasy mystery plot: the magic rules in Mage make it really easy for players to uncover mysteries. Finding the McGuffin becomes pretty easy with Correspondence. Finding out What Happened is not that hard when you have Time 2.<br /> <br /> Edit: To head off another iteration of the same debates--yes, the Technocracy creates and facilitates a lot of change. But a Technocracy <i>story</i> is more likely to center around stopping a thing. Not always, of course. There are disagreements and is dynamism among Technocrats, just like sometimes thing-stoppage makes sense for mystic mages. I'm speaking in generalities here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 07-19-2017, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T08:58:46-07:00","id":1118187,"title":"","content":"Instead of the status quo, think about a new equilibrium point if you want the game to be dynamic. Sure, big bad thing comes out of the night and the PCs have to stop it, but just going back to the status quo is more like an episodic TV show like Star Trek. If you go with a new equilibrium point, the PCs stopped the big bad thing and are changed by that. Maybe there's a subtle change to society and maybe all of the changes are in the mages, but it's more fun to have a game change.<br /> <br /> You can mix proactive and reactive scenes in any game. My preference is to have my various factions and antagonists developed enough so that they act regardless of whether the PCs act. That means a Nephandi cabal planning on bringing more hate to the city would keep working on their dastardly plans to empower hate groups. If the Nephandi's plans were thwarted, they would have plans to resolve their failures. So, let's say the PCs get one of the mouthpiece racists the Nephandi use captured. The Nephandi cabal would have another minion they could promote, or recruit another.<br /> <br /> Also, most mages are going to know to take precautions to make it harder to do magic. Correspondence and Time are powerful, but subtle mages tend to make it harder to find them. For mages who use cameras as part of their Correspondence effect, foes who know how to avoid the camera are going to be hard to see. The mage might have to use a more vulgar effect or give up the chase.<br /> <br /> For the OP, what are your big bads and what do they want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T08:32:56-07:00","id":1118577,"title":"","content":"The big bads are 5 to 7 (not sure yet) Demon gods who were trapped in a power draining dimension for thousands of years, Greatly weakened, They escaped 13 years ago and have been building up their power base in this strange new world. Their hatred of the characters comes from the fact that they are are the descendants of the mages who trapped them. I plan to have a lot of filler episodes between adventures where they confront the big bads or their minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T11:08:01-07:00","id":1118628,"title":"","content":"Ok, so the PCs are ultimately fighting the Nephandi. I'd say start with the idea of 7 if you know the aspects of the demons and you can always cut down to 5 or 6 by having one of the other demons destroy the other one. Demons don't play nice.<br /> <br /> Since you have new players with characters who are fairly new to being mages, I'd start with minions and reveal gradually. If you go with something like Buffy the Vampire Slayer, different demons could be different 'seasonal' big bads for major story arcs. Clearly there will need to be some ancient writings to decipher and weird signs left by demons who have minions but don't really get how this world works. If you could pull up some Jodi Blake statistics, she might work nicely as a coordinator for one or more of the demons. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:34:23-07:00","id":1118665,"title":"","content":"Yeah, definitely some Neph cults showing up. I may need help statting the Big Bads. I need them to be really tough but possible to defeat. As new to running this as I am, I'm afraid I'll make them way too tough or too weak. I'm either basing them off my take on the elements(fire,water,earth,air,spirit,time,space) or the seven deadly sins. At this point I'm not even sure whether they're corporeal or possessing entities. It'll be a while before they show up in person, so I have a little time to brainstorm and tweak their stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:49:34-07:00","id":1118669,"title":"","content":"Well, if it's a big bad, remember you don't need to give it stats until it is time to fight it. Goals and how the minions are recruited and what they can do are more significant than stats for a mastermind villain fought in the end.<br /> <br /> One great thing about the Kingdoms of Kalamar campaign setting, a D&amp;D campaign setting, is that most of the major adversaries in the world have a little history and you know their power base, but not their stats. The pseudo-Roman Emperor, Kabori, is a military genius trying to rebuild a falling empire. He's also capable of ordering his soldiers to great acts of brutality, such as burning whole villages that protest his rule. Is Kabori evil, is he good, is he lawful, is he chaotic--those questions are left up to the GM.<br /> <br /> If you go with the elements, then your minions could be devotees to darker versions of those elements. Make the fire minions pyromaniacs, water minions to be found of drowning people or giving everyone boating a personal introduction to ravenous sharks, the earth folks into earthquakes and live burials, and so forth. Some of those minions could be spirits and others could be people.<br /> <br /> If you go with the sins, then the minions are exemplars of those sins, or at least enjoy pretending one sin over others. Jodi Blake could easily do Lust, as that's one of her major Nephandic methods to get control of people.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T12:55:09-07:00","id":1118670,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Think I'm going with the elements.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:21:09-07:00","id":1118700,"title":"","content":"If 7 is too many, you can probably scrap one or more of the more esoteric trilogy of spirit, time and space. On the other hand, the Umbra can be a very cool place, so spirit might be one to keep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:42:45-07:00","id":1118706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113343-starting-a-chronicle-in-a-week-any-advice?p=1118670#post1118670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! Think I'm going with the elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the version of the elements you have, but why not do both that AND the seven sins? Give each one a sin (as a core trait, easier to discover) then when they face it, reveal the element it's tied to? I like the idea of finding out that something is ethereal and flying only when you come to face it. Maybe it's my past Anime fan speaking but I say do both, multi-layered mythologies on a single baddie is always cool to me :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T15:19:11-07:00","id":1118720,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty good idea, Eyrelliah, I think I might just run with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:54:06-07:00","id":1118758,"title":"","content":"What do you think of these pairings? Fire/wrath, air/envy, water/lust, earth/sloth, spirit/pride, time/greed, and space/gluttony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T00:51:50-07:00","id":1118861,"title":"","content":"Yeah that works in my mind, you can get quite wiggy with that. The only way to draw out and defeat gluttony is with a simultaneous ritual over a vast space, etc. <br /> By the way the Asian system of elements as detailed in Akashic book has a rock-paper-scissors format in it - always thought that was cool :-) have you thought about doing something similar with yours?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T01:50:20-07:00","id":1118866,"title":"","content":"Just thought about it myself, go for spirit beats time beats space, then have spirit defeated by earth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T09:30:45-07:00","id":1118995,"title":"","content":"Maybe so, I'll think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T05:36:02-07:00","id":1121268,"title":"","content":"To make it a perfect Rock Paper Scissors scenario, you need each sin/element to have three they are strong against, and three they are weak against.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could do what fire emblem did in later versions with their magic. Have three elements have a Rock Paper Scissors relationship (for example, Water beats Fire beats Earth beats Water. Have all those things be be weak to something else (for example, Time), have that thing only weak to one other thing (for example, Space) and have that beatable by the original RPS, any of them.<br /> <br /> So it would look like this. ((Fire -&gt; Earth -&gt; Water -&gt; Fire)) These are the Elements<br /> <br /> Time -&gt; Elements -&gt; Space -&gt; Time<br /> <br /> This is just an example, you can mess around with this as much as you want to make the thematic components line up.<br /> <br /> If you want your game to have a more biblical bent, then you could always arranges the sins in hierarchical order as written in Dante's Inferno.<br /> <br /> The order, from least offensive to most offensive, goes as follows:<br /> <br /> Sloth<br /> Lust<br /> Gluttony<br /> Greed<br /> Wrath<br /> Envy<br /> Pride<br /> <br /> If you wanted to fill out the sphere list, you could add a few more from Dante's Inferno, such as Heresy, Treachery, Fraud, or Violence.<br /> There's a tonne of good stuff out there that can be adapted in whatever mould fits your story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T19:47:00-07:00","id":1121673,"title":"","content":"Seeing the new paradigms, practices, and foci material in the Mage 20 Book of Secrets and knowing that the Mage background material is pretty difficult to grasp as a new player, I'd suggest being a bit loose on paradigms at the beginning. Let the players get how their characters do magick over time. I know when I first played, my character was pretty lame on paradigm. In fact, Gerd Zauberei, due to being a vague PC and a series of poor rolls, became the Adept of Ineptitude. Now that I've spent years with the game, run a few campaigns and borrowed Mage ideas for other games, I'm a lot better on making characters with clear paradigms.<br /> <br /> It may not be how everyone plays the game, but if you want to get immersed and not play mages throwing spheres around like superheroes, it helps to develop how the character's magick works. This requires time.<br /> <br /> One rule I find useful for any tabletop RPG is to assume anything said at the table, unless incredibly tangential to the game, is said by the character a person is playing. This helps remind players not to communicate out-of-character and that if they make asides or nonsequitirs, the game will move on. In a game like Mage, where reality is being defined by how people perceive it, almost any odd remark could have been said in character. I couple this 'what's said at the table is said in character' rule with a reminder when we start the game and when we are on breaks. So, if we stop and eat, it's not an in-character conversation.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I don't know if you have others at the game site or dropping by, but definitely consider what they will hear when you play and whether they will disrupt the game. The best game I played in was a year-long Vampire/Mage game. We basically were in character for all 6 hours or so we played each week, and even though my friends were pretty cool with people dropping by, on game night people who wanted to visit knew to just go to the computer or the fridge unless someone was on a break.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:35:09-07:00","id":1121908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113343-starting-a-chronicle-in-a-week-any-advice?p=1121268#post1121268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want your game to have a more biblical bent, then you could always arranges the sins in hierarchical order as written in Dante's Inferno.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Dante Alighieri's <i>Inferno</i> really be considered 'biblical'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:54:46-07:00","id":1121918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1113343-starting-a-chronicle-in-a-week-any-advice?p=1118758#post1118758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think of these pairings? Fire/wrath, air/envy, water/lust, earth/sloth, spirit/pride, time/greed, and space/gluttony.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter two give me interesting ideas.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a demon that is constantly busy and abhors redundant statements and empty words, because he is literally a miser of time. Time is money for him, literally. The type of demon who will give orders to his infernalist follows that are straight and to the point, and who will become angry if he has to repeat himself (because they wasted his time by not listening well enough). His goals revolve around swindling people out of their personal time - and I mean in the sense that when he gives them something, he takes actual time as payment. The poor mortal blinks and finds that forty hours just passed they can't remember, because they didn't exist during that time. At the height of the demon's power, he was altering history by grabbing up people's pasts - hours at a time - in order to add to his coffers, changing how events played out by the person's absence.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of a demon that eats space. He's mostly a huge, gaping maw, in which vast quantities of empty space are contained. The kind of creature that doesn't travel by moving, but by consuming the space in front of him, until his destination is right there. Of course, because of the bottomless space he's consumed, he's terribly hungry also for things to fill it. So naturally, he eats everything else in front of him. I'm imagining an enormous worm, burrowing through the earth by eating it. And maybe the PCs get swallowed, and end up in a mass of matter floating in space. Lumps of raw earth, with heaps of concrete, boulders, cars and subway trains, and peasant houses sitting on it. And towering above it all is a medieval castle, which once belonged to a wizard until said magus gained the demon's ire. The PCs can raid the wizard's study for books and magical items, if they want. But they're also guarded by whatever magical defenses the wizard put in place. The island as a whole is also populated by the emaciated, half-mad cultists who failed the demon, and who want nothing more than to hunt the PCs down for their delicious meat.<br /> <br /> Because of course a demon of gluttony would have starving cultists trapped in his gullet. That's just thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> Edit: Come to think of it, the wizard's study might hold the answer for how to escape the demon's stomach. The PCs reach the study, only to find the skeleton of the wizard slumped in his chair, having died of hunger, thirst, or simple old age, centuries ago (assuming he had the means to conjure food and water, so he persisted until his natural death). And on the work desk before him, his bony fingers rest on a journal, containing the instructions for a Ritual that could be used to escape, but that the wizard couldn't enact before his death. So, the PCs have to perform the ritual...all while most crazed cultists are on their way, intent on eating them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 07-28-2017, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}